Expanding the <cross product> componentwise gives
$$
(1,2,3)^T\times(3,2,1)^T
=(2-6,\ 9-1,\ 2-6)^T
=\boxed{(-4,8,-4)^T}.
$$
Its <dot product> with each original <vector> is zero, as required.

= b
{parent=1}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

First $(1,-1,0)^T\times(0,0,1)^T=(-1,-1,0)^T$. Taking the remaining <cross product> gives
$$
(1,2,0)^T\times(-1,-1,0)^T=\boxed{(0,0,1)^T}.
$$
The order of the two <cross products> matters because the operation is not associative.

